# Backend

- Python + FastAPI. All database access goes through SQLAlchemy with dialect-portable types; no SQLite-only SQL.
- Every schema change gets an Alembic revision with a working downgrade. The API never creates tables at startup.
- API failures use the error envelope in `app/contracts.py` (`code`, `message`, optional `details`, optional `requestId`). Never return stack traces, paths, SQL, or secrets.
- `app/contracts.py` and `frontend/src/contracts.ts` change together in the same commit.
- Lyric line `index` is zero-based with no gaps. Timing fields, including `startSeconds`, are rejected.
- `POST /api/import` is not registered.
- Tests use real SQLite in `tmp_path`, never a mock database.
- Do not import LangChain or LangGraph. There is no authoring package and no second draft path.
- Lyric generation lives in `app/generation/`. Hiragana and romaji live in `app/reading.py`. Saved songs live in `app/services/` and `app/repositories/`.
- Run backend commands from `backend/` with `uv run`.
